meta {
  name: Invite User
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/users/invite
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "newmember@agency.local",
    "first_name": "New",
    "last_name": "Member",
    "employee_id": "EMP-999",
    "designation_id": "{{designationId}}",
    "system_role": "Staff"
  }
}

docs {
  ### Invite User
  Invites a new staff/team member to the organization.

  **Authentication:** Requires `access_token` and `user.manage` permission.

  **Request Body:**
  - `email` (string, required): New user email address.
  - `first_name` (string, required): User first name.
  - `last_name` (string, required): User last name.
  - `employee_id` (string, required): Unique organization employee ID.
  - `designation_id` (string, required): UUID/ID of designation (job title).
  - `system_role` (enum, optional): System role (`Staff`, `Manager`, `Admin`, default: `Staff`).

  **Response:**
  - `201 Created`: Creates inactive user (`is_active = false`), generates invite token, and dispatches invite notification.
  - `400 Bad Request`: Returned if email or employee_id already exists.
  - `403 Forbidden`: Returned if authenticated user lacks `user.manage` permission.
}
